        <mxCell id="dvz7KDq_2vct3IUIVs_H-19" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;autosize=1;resizable=0;" value="Multi Core" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="80" x="300" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dvz7KDq_2vct3IUIVs_H-20" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="External&lt;br&gt;Memory&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;DDR" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="60" x="755" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dvz7KDq_2vct3IUIVs_H-21" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Data Flow:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. Task assignment: The host&amp;nbsp;sends instructions to the NPU&#39;s command queue &amp;amp; decoding. It cotrol all component in NPU&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Data Fetch:&amp;nbsp;command queue &amp;amp; decoding&amp;nbsp;instructs the DMA (Direct Memory Access)&amp;nbsp;fetch the required inputs (weights,...) from DRAM.&amp;nbsp;DMA efficiently transfers these into the NPU’s on-chip buffer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. Computation:&amp;nbsp;Once data is ready, the Control Unit activates the PE Array (Processing Element Array)&amp;nbsp;performing multiply-accumulate (MAC) operations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4.&amp;nbsp;Result Write-back:&amp;nbsp;After computation, final outputs&amp;nbsp;are written back to the chip buffer.&amp;nbsp; DMA tranfer to DRAM&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="715" x="77.5" y="840" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dvz7KDq_2vct3IUIVs_H-22" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="PE" vertex="1">
